{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535100-does-tremere-s-ghouls-have-it-better-in-v5","id":1535100,"title":"Does Tremere's ghouls have it better? (in V5)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-03T05:59:22-07:00","id":1535100,"title":"Does Tremere's ghouls have it better? (in V5)","content":"At least for the purposes of maintaining forming/maintaining a blood bond? <br /> <br /> Since Tremeres in V5 need to feed their ghouls with vitae, an additional number of times equal to the vampire\u2019s Bane Severity for the bond to form. And a vampire's vitae is extremely addictive... <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bDoes this means Tremere ghouls get to have their &quot;fix&quot; more often then ghouls of other clan's? <br /> <br /> How they are threated is a different matter of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T16:45:36-07:00","id":1535118,"title":"","content":"It would make sense that the Tremere would have to feed there ghouls more frequently than the other clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T18:31:05-07:00","id":1535205,"title":"","content":"Even for Tremere, a single Rouse check is enough to turn a mortal into a ghoul, and Tremere ghouls need only the single Rouse check's worth per month for sustenance.<br /> <br /> How they're treated is entirely pertinent to the conversation. Even with the Pyramid broken, we're still talking about paranoid doomsday preppers who guard their secrets and assets with collective ferocity only seen elsewhere among Nosferatu. Houses Ipsissimus and Carna are only more progressive and permissive by way of comparison to Tremere and Goratrix; in every other circumstance relevant to this conversation, the apple doesn't fall far from the tree.<br /> <br /> By merit of what they do, Tremere ghouls are privy to at least some of those secrets and assets, however minor...while Tremere cannot rely on the blood bond alone to keep ghouls under control. Ergo, they must fall back on <i>other</i> means, including judicious use of Auspex, Dominate, and Blood Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T14:00:42-07:00","id":1535229,"title":"","content":"Indeed the Tremere in clan disciplines would more then make up for the weakness of the blood bond they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T18:17:43-07:00","id":1535236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535100-does-tremere-s-ghouls-have-it-better-in-v5?p=1535229#post1535229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed the Tremere in clan disciplines would more then make up for the weakness of the blood bond they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> The V5 iteration of Domitor's Favor has been panned in some places as being comparatively weak to what it used to do, versus the discipline level it is in V5 and the powers against which it competes. I won't say it isn't lackluster in most circumstances taking into account blood bonds being capped to blood potency, but in Tremere hands it becomes <i>very</i> useful on account of the clan bane. It honestly kind of flips the script, from one apprentice in the chantry being charged with keeping watch over ghouls, to the Regent themselves given they're certainly going to be the one with the highest potency and therefore able to sustain more bonds.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, given Tremere discipline array they hardly <i>need</i> the bond. Tremere ghouls would likely be disinclined to go rogue after seeing a mortal dominated to drink scorpionated blood, or microwaved from the inside out, by a perturbed Regent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T12:45:12-07:00","id":1535295,"title":"","content":"Be nice and do what your told or Corbin here will make you regret with whatever new blood sorcery ritual that he is trying out and wants a lab rat to work on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T04:42:15-07:00","id":1535436,"title":"","content":"I never quite thought of the alternative options Tremeres have instead of relying on the blood bond. Weakening their blood with the v5 clan bane, kinda makes them even more scarier and creative in the application of their powers and methods to maintain control.<br /> <br /> So a Tremere ghoul must be exceptionally useful/valuable enough that a Tremere is willing to invest their vitae in maintaining a blood bond.<br /> <br /> My initial impressions of the v5 clan bane is colored by fellow players impression that Tremeres are now just walking blood banks for other Kindred. Since they(Tremeres) can be fed on without the risk of being blood bonded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","user":"Wingstorm","date":". 05-11-2024, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T05:59:13-07:00","id":1535439,"title":"","content":"The bond still forms, it just takes significantly longer for a Tremere to bond a mortal. It's still <i>maintained</i> at the same cost as other vampires. Thus, it's more an issue of &quot;how do I maintain control over this mortal in the short-term&quot; than it is &quot;how do I maintain control over this mortal altogether&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given Tremere ghouling preferences -- which have yet to be published in V5 of which I'm aware, leaving us to fall back to earlier editions -- that's paramount, as the mortals they prefer tend towards willfulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T12:17:26-07:00","id":1535520,"title":"","content":"In many ways Tremere ghouls might have a worse time then other clan ghouls as it's been mentioned that the Tremere vitae has been changed by the destruction of there main headquarters and most of the leadership and perhaps Saulot is trying something different with his current clan to cull the useless from them and this is one method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T23:10:10-07:00","id":1536933,"title":"","content":"In a Clan that has Dominate, and a strict authoritarian social structure? No. The only ghouls who maybe have it worse are of Clan Lasombra, who are social Darwinists, and hate any form of subservience, which they see as weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 06-08-2024, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}